$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Step 1. 6-Bromodihydrobenzofuran (44) (2.39 g,
12.02 mmol), 3-mercaptopropionic acid 2-ethyhexyl ester (52) (2.76 g,
12.6 mmol), Pd2dba3 (165 mg, 0.180 mmol), and xantphos (279 mg, 0.481
mmol) were placed in a flask followed by degassed dioxane (40 mL) and
Hünig's base (4.2 mL, 0.18 mol) under nitrogen. The mixture was heated at
100 °C for 10 h, cooled to room temperature, diluted with CH2Cl2,
filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by SiO2
chromatography (EtOAc/hexane, 0- 30%) to afford of 2-ethylhexyl
3-(2,3-dihydro-1-benzofuran-6-ylthio)propanoate. 2-Ethylhexyl
3-[(6-Chloro-1,3-benzodioxol-5-yl)sulfanyl]-propanoate (43c). The title
compound was prepared in 92% yield from 41c and 52 in a manner similar to
that described for 45, step 1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of
(2S)-1-[4-(2-{6-Amino-8-[(6-bromo-1,3-benzodioxol-5-yl)sulfanyl]-9H-purin-9-yl}ethyl)piperidin-1-yl]-2-hydroxypropan-1-one
(MPC-3100), a Purine-Based Hsp90 Inhibitor
