$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM ethyl 4-(2-(methoxycarbonyl)phenylthio)-3-nitrobenzoate (7). 6 (4.67 ml,
34 mmol) was added during 30 min to a mixture of 5 (6.60 g, 30.9 mmol)
and Cs2CO3 (10.06 g, 30.9 mol) in DMF (60 mL) at 40 °C. The reaction
mixture was diluted with ethyl acetate and water after additional 15 min
(full conversion according to TLC). The aqueous phase was extracted once
with ethyl acetate and the combined organic phases were washed twice with
water followed by brine and dried (Na2SO4). Filtration and concentration
of the organic phase at reduced pressure gave a yellow crystalline
residue. Recrystallization from ethyl acetate/heptane gave 7 (10.3 g,
92%) as yellow crystals ethyl
4-(2-(methoxycarbonyl)phenylthio)-3-nitrobenzoate (7), (10.3 g, 92%)
yield 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.82 (d, 1H, J = 1.9), 7.94 (m, 2H),
7.62-7.57 (m, 3H), 6.92 (d, 1H, J = 8.6), 4.38 (q, 2H, J = 7.2), 3.78 (s,
3H), 1.38 (t, 3H, J = 7.0); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 166.8, 164.6,
145.5, 144.1, 137.6, 136.3, 133.4, 133.0, 131.5, 131.3, 130.5, 129.8,
128.1, 126.9, 61.9, 52.7, 14.5.
