$DATUM 4-(2-Methoxycarbonyl-phenylsulfanyl)-3-nitro-benzoic acid ethyl ester:
Cs2CO3 (10.06 g, 30.9 mmol) was added to a solution of ethyl
4-flouro-3-nitrobenzoate (6.60 g, 30.9 mmol) and methyl
2-mercaptobenzoate (4.67 ml, 34 mmol) in DMF (60 ml) and the resulting
mixture was stirred for 2 hours at 40 °C. The reaction mixture was cooled
to room temperature and diluted with DCM (60 ml). The organic phase was
washed with water and dried (Na2SO4). Filtration, removal of the solvent
at reduced pressure and column chromatography (ethyl acetate/heptane 1:4)
gave a yellow crystalline residue. Recrystallization from EtOAc-heptane
gave 10.3 g (92%) of the title compound as yellow crystals.
4-(2-Methoxycarbonyl-phenylsulfanyl)-3-nitro-benzoic acid ethyl ester,
yield 10.3 g (92%) M.p. 117-119 °C.1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.82 (d, 1H,
J = 1.9 Hz), 7.94 (m, 2H), 7.62-7.57 (m, 3H), 6.92 (d, 1H, J = 8.6 Hz),
4.38 (q, 2H, J = 7.2 Hz), 3.78 (s, 3H), 1.38 (t, 3H, J = 7.0 Hz); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 166.8, 164.6, 145.5, 144.1, 137.6, 136.3, 133.4,
133.0, 131.5, 131.3, 130.5, 129.8, 128.1, 126.9, 61.9, 52.7, 14.5; HRMS
(Ion Mode: FAB+) m/z [M+H+] Calcd for C17H15NO6S, 362.0698; Found,
362.0701.
