$DATUM 4-(Phenylthio)benzaldehyde (S41). A solution of 4-fluorobenzaldehyde (2.2
g, 17.7 mmol, 1 equiv) in anhydrous DMF (25 mL) was treated with
benzenethiol (1.7 mL, 16.6 mmol, 0.93 equiv) and K2CO3 (2.8 g, 20.3 mmol,
1.14 equiv). After stirring for 5 h at 130 °C, the reaction mixture was
washed with saturated aqueous NH4Cl and extracted with EtOAc. The organic
layer was dried over Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated. Column
chromatography (SiO2, 4 x 7 cm, 10% EtOAc-hexanes) afforded S41 as a
yellow oil. 4-(Phenylthio)benzaldehyde, yield 3.45 g, 16.1 mmol, 91%. 1H
NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 9.91 (s, 1H), 7.72 (d, 2H, J = 8.2 Hz), 7.55-7.52
(m, 2H), 7.44-7.42 (m, 2H), 7.24 (d, 2H, J = 8.2 Hz); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100
MHz) δ 191.2, 147.2, 134.3, 133.6, 131.2, 130.1, 129.8, 129.1, 127.1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Structure-Activity Relationships of α-Ketooxazole Inhibitors of Fatty
