$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (2-nitro-phenyl)-phenyl ether (3a)
(2-nitro-phenyl)-(4-methoxylphenyl) sulfide (3h). Following above
procedure, 4-methoxyl benzenethiol (4.20g, 30mmol), KOH (1.68g, 30mmol)
and 1-chloro-2-nitro-benzene (4.72g, 30mmol) were used. 3h (7.12g) was
obtained as a yellow powder in 91% yield. 1H NMR (300MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.24
(dd, J = 6.0, 8.1 Hz , 1H, Ar-H); 7.51 (d, 2H, J = 8.7 Hz, Ar-H); 7.34
