$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Representative Procedure. Under an atmosphere of N2, a borosilicate glass
tube was charged in turn with CuI (0.10 mmol, 10%), NaOt-Bu (1.0 mmol,
1.0 equiv), CH3CN (3.0 mL), the aryl halide (1.0 mmol, 1.0 equiv), and
the aryl thiol (1.0 mmol, 1.0 equiv). The tube was sealed with a rubber
septum, and then the heterogeneous reaction mixture was stirred at 0 °C,
irradiating with a 100 W Hg lamp. After 5-24 h, the volatiles were
removed under reduced pressure. The residue was suspended in Et2O, and
the mixture was filtered through a short plug of Celite. The filtrate was
concentrated, and the residue was purified by column chromatography.
3,5-Dimethylphenyl phenyl sulfide (Table 2, entry 1) [457625-29-5].
According to the general procedure, 1-iodo-3,5-dimethylbenzene (144 μL,
1.0 mmol, 1.0 equiv) and thiophenol (103 μL, 1.0 mmol, 1.0 equiv) were
reacted at 0 °C for 5 h. The product (colorless oil) was purified by
column chromatography (SiO2, hexanes). Run 1: 194 mg (91% yield).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM photochemical, Hg lamp used, sealed tube used, alternative reaction
conditions gave lower yield, scalable, optimization study, optimized on
catalyst and base
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A New Family of Nucleophiles for Photoinduced, Copper-Catalyzed
