$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
Diphenylsulfide (entry 1, table 2): To a solution of CoI2 (dppe)(0.0050
mmol), zinc (0.750 mmol), pyridine (0.50 mmol) and iodobenzene (0.50
mmol) were added thiophenol (0.50 mmol) and CH3CN (2.0 mL). The reaction
mixture was allowed to stir at 80 °C for 10 h. At the end of the
reaction, the reaction mixture was diluted with CH2Cl2, filtered through
Celite and silica gel. The filtrate was concentrated and the residue was
purified through a silica gel column using Ethyl acetate and hexane as
eluent. Cyclohexyl(p-tolyl)sulfide as colorless oil, yield 91%. 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 1.30-1.34 (m, 5H), 1.57-1.58 (m, 1H), 1.72-1.75 (m,
2H), 1.92-1.96 (m, 2H), 2.30 (s, 3H), 2.98-2.99 (m, 1H), 7.07 (d, J = 8.0
Hz, 2H), 7.29 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H) ; 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 21.1,
25.8, 26.1 (2C), 33.4 (2C), 47.1, 129.5 (2C), 131.2, 132.8 (2C), 136.8;
HRMS calcd for C13H18S 206.1129 found 206.1129.
