$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The mixture of anilines (8.75 g, 34.86 mmol) was added to a solution of
O-ethylxanthic acid, potassium salt (33.47 g, 52.3 mmol) in DMF (150 mL)
and heated to 160 °C for 4 h. Only aniline reacted to form compound
7-bromobenzothiazole-2-thiol. The reaction mixture was cooled to room
temperature, and the solvent was removed in vacuo. The crude material was
suspended in NH4Cl (saturated) and the precipitate collected on a filter,
washed with water (50 mL x 2), and dried under vacuum to give product
7-bromobenzothiazole-2-thiol, yield 91%. white solid, 1HNMR (CD3OD) δ
7.21 (t, J = 6.3 Hz, 1H), 7.29 (d, J = 6.3 Hz, 1H), 7.34 (d, J = 7.3 Hz,
1H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM thermal, key step
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM 7'-Substituted Benzothiazolothio- and Pyridinothiazolothio-Purines as
Potent Heat Shock Protein 90 Inhibitors
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zhang, Lin; Fan, Junhua; Vu, Khang; Hong, Kevin; Le Brazidec, Jean-Yves;
Shi, Jiandong; Biamonte, Marco; Busch, David J.; Lough, Rachel E.;
