$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: From 1-Thioglycoses 2a, 2d-2g: To a
well-stirred suspension of K2CO3 (0.2 g) in acetone (20 mL) were added
sequentially 1-thioglycose (1 mmol), 4-nitrofluorobenzene (3b; 1.1 mmol)
and H2O (0.1 mL). The resulting mixture was stirred at r.t. for 0.3-4h
(Table), diluted with CH2Cl2 (20 mL), filtered and the solution was
evaporated. The expected compound was isolated by crystallization from
EtOH. 4c, yield 91%. mp (°C) found:203-204; reported: 200-201; [α]D found
(c, CHCl3): - 96 (0.5) ; reported : -104; 13C NMR (CDCl3/TMS), δ (sugar
ring carbons): 83.2 (C-1), 76.4, 73.5, 69.2, 68.0, 62.2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
