$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-tert-Butyl 4-Ethyl
4-{[4-(Phenylthio)phenyl]sulfonyl}-piperidine-1,4-dicarboxylate (36). To
a solution of sulfone 30 (40 g, 96 mmol) and powdered K2CO3 (26 g, 188
mmol) in DMF (200 mL) cooled to 0 °C was added thiophenol (19.8 mL, 192
mmol), and the resulting composition was then stirred at room temperature
for 36 h. That solution was concentrated under high vacuum, and the
residue was dissolved in EA. The organic layer was washed with H2O and
dried over MgSO4. Chromatography on silica gel eluting with EA/hexane
provided the phenylthiophenyl BOC-sulfone 36 as a white solid (44.3 g,
91%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
