$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-(Benzylsulfanyl)-6-methoxybenzaldehyde (37). To a suspension of sodium
tert-butoxide (3.47 g, 36.1 mmol) in THF (50 mL) was added
benzylmercaptan (4.24 mL, 32.2 mmol) at 0 °C and the mixture was stirred
at 0 °C for 30 minutes. To the reaction mixture was added dropwise a
solution of 2-fluoro-6-methoxybenzaldehyde (36, 4.64 g, 30.1 mmol) in THF
(10 mL) and the mixture was stirred at room temperature for 1 h. To the
reaction mixture was added water (150 mL) and the resulting precipitate
was collected by filtration. The collected solid was washed with water
(20 mL) and Et2O (50 mL) successively and dried in vacuo to give 37.
(7.08 g, 91%), pale yellow solid. 1HNMR (CDCl3) δ 3.91 (3H, s), 4.15 (2H,
s), 6.72 (1H, d, J = 8.3 Hz), 6.95 (1H, J = 8.3 Hz), 7.25 -7.43 (6H, m),
10.59 (1H, s).
