$DATUM (2-Fluoro-5-methoxy-4-nitrophenyl)(methyl)sulfane (68). To
1,2-difluoro-4-methoxy-5-nitrobenzene (67, 0.72 g, 3.8 mmol) in EtOH (100
mL) was added sodium thiomethoxide (0.30 g, 4.1 mmol) in water (0.96 mL,
53 mmol), and the reaction mixture was heated to reflux for 3 h. The
solvent was removed under reduced pressure and the residue was purified
by flash chromatography, 0-40% EtOAc/ heptane, to afford the title
compound. Yield (0.75 g, 91%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.68 (d, J= 9.3
Hz, 1H), 6.83 (d, J= 6.1 Hz, 1H), 3.98 (s, 3H), 2.55 (s, 3H). LCMS, m/z =
not detected.
