$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical procedure for coupling a carboxylic
acid with SPPSLHMP (0.16 μmol) SynPhase Lanterns® : a mixture of DMAP
(0.02 M), DIC (0.2 M), carboxylic acid (0.2 M) and SynPhase Lanterns® in
DMF/DCM (0.5 ml each per Lantern) was stirred at 50°C for 15 hours. The
SynPhase Lanterns® were washed with DMF (3 x 5ml per Lantern) and DCM (3
x 5 ml per Lantern). Typical procedure for coupling reaction of thiols :
a mixture of thiol (0.25M), (bpy)2NiBr2 (0.05eq), borohydride polymer
supported Amberlite® IRA400 (2.5 mmol/g) (0.5 M) and SynPhase Lanterns®
in EtOH/THF (1 ml per Lantern) was stirred at 70°C in a reactor fitted
with a polypropylene gauze to avoid contact between SynPhase Lanterns®
and resin for 15h. SynPhase Lanterns® were washed with THF (3 x with 5 ml
per Lantern), EtOH (5 ml per Lantern) and DCM (3 x 5 ml per Lantern).
Information not present.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported reaction (; HMP SynPhase polystrene lanterns used ; first
stage is attachment to resin ; solid-supported reagent ; IRA-400
borohydride resin used)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
